A||||6||Ed||Car Show (and dew wipes, and Fiero Shop)||||1||
Z||000000||Ed||11-16-2000||09:21 PM||||Went to a new car show today.  STICKER SHOCK!<P>Its good to go to these once in while.  It cooled off my desire for a Porsche.  $50,000 for the cheap one (boxster) and $80,000 for the good one (Carrera).  Hummers are pretty nice too at $100,000 and Ferraris at $150,000 (but a $100,000 mark up if you want it now!).  <BR>Besides, there wasn't even enough headroom for me in the Carrera.  And forget the tech discussion forum here.  It looks essentially impossible to work on any of these yourselves.  I asked to see the engine of the Boxster, and the rep said it would take 20 minutes to get to it.  A lot of trunk room, though.    <P>MR2's looked nice, but they have about 5 cubic feet of storage, a lot less than our highly criticized Fieros.  The Hondas were nice, though at $10,000 more than the MR2.  <P>I guess I'll find a few bucks to hot up my GT and not worry about a new something.<P>P.S.  Did the dew wipes.  Three of us with the professional supervision of George Miller at his Fiero Shop in Richmond, CA did one side in about 1 1/2 hours but the second only took about 1/2 hour.  <P>I recommend his shop and tech sessions to northern CA forum members.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||11-16-2000||10:28 PM||||While at the gas station today, the Vector(yellow, see it around town a couple times a week) pulled in, and started filling up on on island opposite to me. Temps were in the 40's, he must have had it out for one last drive before he parks it for winter. That thing looks so sweet, but maintanance must be a fortune. It sounds real good too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||11-16-2000||10:44 PM||||Ed, sorry I missed you at the tech session! I usually go out of town on the weekends - working here with George all week drives me to insanity (just kidding George!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) -- I do hope to see you at some of our (CFOG) get-togethers from time to time -- did recieve your email about stopping in Paso Robles sometime -- usually catch me there on the weekends but through the week I am at the shop slaving........errrrrr.......working hard!!<P>Glad you changed those dew wipes!! that's one job that just isn't my favorite - wanna come back and put in a sunroof??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Oh, and, put your money into the GT!!! more bang for the buck, right??<P>------------------<BR>                  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                              <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||11-16-2000||11:12 PM||||Yep! We all drive a good value. My 2.8 L is fine and running well.  When it wears out it will be replaced with something in the V-6 family, and I won't be getting a Porsche! <BR>  <BR>My '87 GT already has a sunroof, but if I get that Ferrino (you can see the "for sale" ad in our newsletter I sent to CFOG and Golden Gate) we can put one on it.  Or are you thinking about yours?  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||11-17-2000||12:18 AM||||nosir.......all of mine already have sunroofs but we can sure do one for the Ferrino! i only said that because I am putting a sunroof on a customer's car (the white one the dew wipes went on) ......... now, if we can just get that 3.4L in it ............<P>------------------<BR>                  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                              <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ed||11-17-2000||12:34 AM||||That's right, now I remember.  The car you're putting the 3.4 L in, and the factory sunroof on, belongs to one of our club members. He's promised to show it off to the rest of the club when its installed.  <P>Looking forward to seeing it completed (and maybe a test drive, Mr. B. C.)?!||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||11-17-2000||02:08 AM||||well........since Bruce is one of your club members I'll have to make sure the sunroof gets an extra coat of RainX......he is really a nice guy and you are fortunate to have him as a member of your club. (that has to be one of the cleanest little '88's I have ever seen!!)||||reg||1
